Gliff for macOS derives from Gliff 0.4.0 by Kevin McConnell (MIT).
See LICENSE and ATTRIBUTION.md; preserve upstream attribution.

The macOS client uses Apple's system VideoToolbox/CoreMedia/CoreVideo frameworks
for H.264 decoding. It does not bundle or download OpenH264 or another codec
module. Apple selects the decoder; hardware acceleration is not guaranteed.
